.SS "struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * stumpless_add_new_param (struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element, const char * param_name, const char * param_value)"

.PP
Creates a new param and adds it to the given element\&. This is equivalent to calling \fBstumpless_new_param()\fP and passing the result directly \fBstumpless_add_param()\fP\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:param_name race:param_value\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that the param name and value or not changed by other threads during execution\&. A mutex is used to coordinate updates to the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access and the use of memory management functions to create the new param\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked as well as memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to add the new param to\&.
.br
\fIparam_name\fP The name of the new param\&.
.br
\fIparam_value\fP The value of the new param\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The modified element if no error is encountered\&. If an error is encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * stumpless_add_param (struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element, struct \fBstumpless_param\fP * param)"

.PP
Adds a param to an element\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate updates to the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access and the use of memory management functions to adjust the array of params in the element\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked as well as memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to add the param to\&.
.br
\fIparam\fP The param to add to element\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The modified element if no error is encountered\&. If an error is encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBExamples\fP
.in +1c
\fBentry_example\&.c\fP, \fBfile_example\&.c\fP, \fBsocket_example\&.c\fP, \fBstream_example\&.c\fP, \fBtcp_example\&.c\fP, and \fBudp_example\&.c\fP\&.
.SS "struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * stumpless_copy_element (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element)"

.PP
Creates a copy of an element\&. Copies of elements are 'deep' in that the copy also copies each of the params that the original element has, if any\&. This means that even if the params of the original element are destroyed, the equivalent ones in this element will still be valid\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate the read of the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access and the use of memory management functions to create the copy\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked as well as memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to copy\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A new element that is a deep copy of the original\&. If an error is encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void stumpless_destroy_element_and_contents (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * e)"

.PP
Destroys an element as well as all params that it contains, freeing any allocated memory\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Unsafe\fP This function is not thread safe as it destroys resources that other threads would use if they tried to reference this struct\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the destruction of a lock that may be in use as well as the use of the memory deallocation function to release memory\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed, and the memory deallocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIe\fP The element to destroy\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBExamples\fP
.in +1c
\fBentry_example\&.c\fP\&.
.SS "void stumpless_destroy_element_only (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element)"

.PP
Destroys an element, freeing any allocated memory\&. Associated params are left untouched, and must be destroyed separately\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Unsafe\fP This function is not thread safe as it destroys resources that other threads would use if they tried to reference this struct\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the destruction of a lock that may be in use as well as the use of the memory deallocation function to release memory\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed, and the memory deallocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to destroy\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "bool stumpless_element_has_param (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element, const char * name)"

.PP
True if the given element has a param with the given name, false otherwise\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name is not changed by another thread during execution\&. A mutex is used to coordinate access to the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to search for the param\&.
.br
\fIname\fP The name of the param to check for\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if no error is encountered and the param is found\&. If the param is not found or an error is encountered, then false is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const char * stumpless_element_to_string (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element)"

.PP
Returns name and params from element as a formatted string\&. The character buffer should be freed when no longer is needed by the caller\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate the read of the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access and the use of memory management functions to create the result\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked as well as memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.2\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to get the name and params from\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The formatted string of name or name=[param1,\&.\&.\&.] if no error is encountered\&. If an error is encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const char * stumpless_get_element_name (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element)"

.PP
Returns the name of the given element\&. The character buffer must be freed by the caller when it is no longer needed to avoid memory leaks\&.
.PP
In versions prior to v2\&.0\&.0, the returned pointer was to the internal buffer used to store the name and was not to be modified by the caller\&. This behavior changed in v2\&.0\&.0 in order to avoid thread safety issues\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate the read of the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access and the use of memory management functions to create the result\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked as well as memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to get the name from\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The name of the element, if no error is encountered\&. If an error is encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "struct \fBstumpless_param\fP * stumpless_get_param_by_index (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element, size_t index)"

.PP
Returns the param in the given element at the specified index\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate access to the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to get the param from\&.
.br
\fIindex\fP The index of the param to retrieve\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The param if no error is encountered\&. If an error is encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
