.SS "struct \fBstumpless_param\fP * stumpless_get_param_by_name (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element, const char * name)"

.PP
Returns the first occurrence of a param with the given name in element, if it is found\&. Note that an element may contain as many instances of a param as desired according to RFC 5424, and therefore there may be other param instances with the same name\&. If you simply need a count of params with a given name, then you can use stumpless_get_param_name_count to find this\&. If you need a reference to any other params, then you must loop through all params in the element using stumpless_get_param_by_index, checking each name\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name is not changed by another thread during execution\&. A mutex is used to coordinate access to the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to search\&.
.br
\fIname\fP The param name to search for\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The param if it is found in the element, or NULL otherwise\&. If an error was encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "size_t stumpless_get_param_count (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element)"

.PP
Returns the number of params in the given element\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate access to the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to get the param count of\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The number of params element has\&. If there is an error, zero is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "size_t stumpless_get_param_index (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element, const char * name)"

.PP
Gives the index of the first occurrence of a param with the given name in the given element\&. Note that an element may contain as many instances of a param as desired according to RFC 5424, and therefore there may be other param instances that this function does not recognize\&. If you simply need a count of params with a given name, then you can use stumpless_get_param_name_count to find this\&. If you need a reference to any other params, then you must loop through all params in the element using stumpless_get_param_by_index, checking each name\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name is not changed by another thread during execution\&. A mutex is used to coordinate access to the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to search for params with the given name\&.
.br
\fIname\fP The name to search params for\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The first instance of a param with name in element, if one exists\&. If there is no such param or an error is encountered, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const char * stumpless_get_param_name_by_index (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element, size_t index)"

.PP
Gets the name of the param with the given index in this element\&. The result character buffer must be freed by the caller when it is no longer needed to avoid memory leaks\&.
.PP
In versions prior to v2\&.0\&.0, the returned pointer was to the internal buffer used to store the name and was not to be modified by the caller\&. This behavior changed in v2\&.0\&.0 in order to avoid thread safety issues\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate the read of the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access and the use of memory management functions to create the result\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked as well as memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to get the param and name from\&.
.br
\fIindex\fP The index of the param to get the name from\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The name of the param at the given index, if no error is encountered\&. If an error is encountered, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "size_t stumpless_get_param_name_count (const struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element, const char * name)"

.PP
Gives the number of params with the given name found in the given element\&. If you need to get an actual reference to any of these params beyond the first one, then you will need to loop through all params in the element using stumpless_get_param_by_index, checking each name\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name is not changed by another thread during execution\&. A mutex is used to coordinate access to the element with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIelement\fP The element to search for params\&.
.br
\fIname\fP The name to look for in params\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The number of params found with the given name in the given element\&. If an error is encountered, zero is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
