.SS "struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * stumpless_load_element (struct \fBstumpless_element\fP * element, const char * name)"

.PP
Loads a provided element with the given name\&. Does not call any memory allocation routines, and is faster than stumpless_new_element as a result\&.
.PP
An element loaded using this function must be unloaded with stumpless_unload_element when it is no longer needed\&. Calling stumpless_destroy_element or any function that does (such as stumpless_destroy_entry_and_contents will result in memory corruption)\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:element race:name\fP This function is thread safe, assuming that the element and name are not changed by other threads during execution\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a mutex initialization routine\&. If STUMPLESS_THREAD_SAFETY_SUPPORTED is not defined, then this function is AS-Safe\&.
